ef57d77   .:/settings/profile .:/etc/hosts.conf .:/etc/app.properties .:/docs/readme.markdown .:/x.template .:/.gitignore R:/api/v1.0 R:/v3.0 .://
a5484ba   R:/settings/profile .:/etc/hosts.conf R:/etc/app.properties R:/docs/readme.markdown R:/x.template R:/.gitignore R:/api/v1.0 R:/v3.0 R://
38fb601   R:/settings/profile .:/etc/hosts.conf R:/etc/app.properties R:/docs/readme.markdown R:/x.template R:/.gitignore R:/api/v1.0 R:/v3.0 R://
eb27489   R:/settings/profile .:/etc/hosts.conf .:/etc/app.properties .:/docs/readme.markdown .:/x.template .:/.gitignore .:/api/v1.0 .:/v3.0 R://
8b33f45   R:/settings/profile .:/etc/hosts.conf .:/etc/app.properties .:/docs/readme.markdown .:/x.template .:/.gitignore R:/api/v1.0 R:/v3.0 .://
--- the two corrected passages, as this commit leaves them ---
77:The last two are measured against 19941ad, the commit before this fix. One holds three lines
78-that the two rounds of route widening broke in turn, each attribution read off ``git show <sha>
79--- plugins/webster/scripts/doctype.py`` rather than remembered. a5484ba, round one, replaced the
80-narrow /api and /v<n> rule with a six-letter cap on the file-extension exclusion, so a path whose
81-extension ran past six — `/etc/app.properties`, `/docs/readme.markdown` — was reported as a
82-route, while `.conf` is four letters, fitted the cap, and never was. The same commit opened the
83-path body on a slash, so `//` became a route with no segment in it. eb27489, round two, lifted
84-that cap to sixteen and admitted digits, which read `.0` as an extension, so `/api/v1.0` and
85-`/v3.0` stopped being reported at all; its path body is byte-identical to a5484ba's. 38fb601
86-never touched ROUTE_PATH. The other reads the printed contract rather than the rule behind it.
343:    Lifting that cap took one more thing with it that this pins as well. eb27489 admitted
344-    digits into the extension, which made `.0` look like one, so `/api/v1.0` and `/v3.0`
345-    stopped being reported — routes the narrow /api and /v<n> rule a5484ba replaced had caught
346-    since ROUTE_PATH was written, which made a fix into a regression. The `//` gap belongs to
347-    a5484ba rather than to the cap-lifting commit: its path body admitted every character but a
348-    backtick or a space, a second slash included, and eb27489 left that body byte-identical.
349-    That made `` `//` `` a path with zero segments when A-008 asks for at least one.
